# ═══════════════════════════════════════════
#  "Soul Brother" — Boom Bap / Sample Chop
#  BeatForge Script Demo Song
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════

bpm 92
swing 45
reverb 0.25
delay 0.15

# ── Drums (classic boom bap) ─────────────
kick  "x......ox..x...."
snare "....x.......x..."
hh    "x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x."
oh    "..............x."
rim   "..x...........x."

# ── Chopped samples ──────────────────────
# Load CHOPS kit (click CHOPS button)
# Amen break chops for fills:
# Use pads 0-7 for amen slices
# Program fills in Bank D:
# amen1 "x...x..x.x..x..x"
# amen3 "..x...x...x...x."

# ── Bass line (Fender-style) ─────────────
note "C2.2 C2.2 ~ ~ Eb2.2 Eb2.2 ~ ~ F2.2 ~ G2.2 ~ Ab2.4 ~ ~ ~"

# ── Soul chords (use Warm Pad preset) ────
# Assign synth on pad 14, select "Warm Pad"
# Piano roll chords (use CHORD stamp tool):
# Step 1: Cm7  (C Eb G Bb)
# Step 5: Fm7  (F Ab C Eb)
# Step 9: Gm7  (G Bb D F)
# Step 13: Fm7 (F Ab C Eb)

# ── Arrangement (classic hip hop) ────────
# Bank A: 4 bars — drums only (establish groove)
# Bank B: 4 bars — add bass + sample chops
# Bank C: 4 bars — add chords (full arrangement)
# Bank D: 2 bars — breakdown (just bass + hats)
# Bank E: 4 bars — back to full + fills
# Bank F: 2 bars — outro (fade drums, keep chords)

# ── Mix philosophy ───────────────────────
# This is a sample-based beat — the samples ARE the song
# Keep it dusty: master enhancer 25%, slight bitcrush on drums
# Vinyl crackle: load a noise sample, set very low volume
# Bass: sidechain to kick, that's the bounce
# Chords: reverb 40%, delay 20% (dreamy)
# Everything through tape saturation (already on master)
